<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="2" to="4" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="b" from="2" to="4" step="1" exclude="$a"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="c" from="1" to="4" step="1" exclude="$a $b"/>
  <function name="k" variable="n">(n + $b)/(2n + $c)</function>
  <function name="genTermf" variables="x n">(n + $b)/(2n + $c)*(n+$a)*x^(n+$a-1)</function>
</setup>

<p>
  Let <m>f(x)</m> be a function whose Taylor series is
  <me>
    f(x) = \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{n + $b}{2n + $c}x^{n+$a}
  </me>
</p>

<p>
  Write out the first 4 nonzero terms of the series for <m>f(x)</m> and apply the Power Series Differentiation and Integration Theorem to find the first four nonzero terms of the series for <m>f'(x)</m> and state those in the provided blanks below.
</p>
<p sectionWideCheckWork forceIndividualAnswerColoring>
  <m>f'(x) = </m><answer>$$k(0)*(0+$a)*x^($a-1)</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$k(1)*($a+1)*x^($a)</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$k(2)*($a+2)*x^($a+1)</answer><m>+</m><answer>$$k(3)*($a+3)*x^($a+2)</answer><m>+ \cdots</m>
</p>
<p>
  Finally, state the Taylor series for <m>f'(x)</m> in sigma notation.
</p>
 <p>
  <m>\displaystyle f'(x) = \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} </m><answer>$genTermf</answer>
</p> 